{"agent_image": null, "agent_image_digest": null, "agent_mode": null, "anthropic_pin": "2.0.50", "binary_hash_source": "post_hoc_disk", "binary_path": "/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode", "binary_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "binary_source": null, "build_channel": "local:build.ts", "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_image": "h2-env:1022@sha256:<REDACTED_HEX>", "cell_seed": 17356979595533457054, "checker_defect": false, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_lock": null, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "", "checker_timeout_s": 120, "checker_wall_time_s": 5.629, "checker_workspace_files": {".ruff_cache/.gitignore": {"bytes": 35, "mtime": 1794522814.24904, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, ".ruff_cache/0.12.5/4500454486557532956": {"bytes": 118, "mtime": 1794523322.629159, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, ".ruff_cache/CACHEDIR.TAG": {"bytes": 43, "mtime": 1794522814.24904, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "check.py": {"bytes": 4412, "mtime": 1793746358.705186, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "gen.py": {"bytes": 7118, "mtime": 1794523322.1911528, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "re.json": {"bytes": 230737, "mtime": 1794523323.483171, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "test.py": {"bytes": 1945, "mtime": 1794522831.481281, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode", "run", "--print-logs", "-m", "anthropic/claude-opus-5-5", "--format", "json", "--title", "openbench", "Write a JSON file called /tmp/obench-cell-v5gzqemy/bench_opencode_regex-chess_d3bcttns/re.json that is a list of [regex, replacement] pairs. When executed in order with the Python code\n```\ndef all_legal_next_positions(fen):\n  for pattern, repl in json.load(open(\"/tmp/obench-cell-v5gzqemy/bench_opencode_regex-chess_d3bcttns/re.json\")):\n      fen = re.sub(pattern, repl, fen)\n  return fen.split(\"\\n\")\n```\nthis function should return the FEN position for all possible legal next chess positions.\n\nMake the following simplifying assumptions:\n- You will only be shown positions where it is white to move\n- Any promotions will only be made to Queen (assume that underpromotion is not a legal move)\n- You do not need to track the full-move or half-move count\n\nThe input will be provided, as a string like \"<REDACTED_B64> w kq - 0 1\".\nWhen run on this string, your answer must produce the following output:\n\"<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\\<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\\<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\"\nNote that the final output of the move and halfmove are allowed to be incorrect. So the above is scored properly even though the move numbers are wrong.\n\nWith these exceptions (and only these exceptions) you must implement a fully correct move generator, including:\n- Castling, with proper tracking of castling rights\n- Promotion, except only allow promotion to queen\n- En-passant\n\nThe length of re.json must be under 100,000 [regex, replacement]-pairs long, and under 10 megabytes in total.\n\nYou can look at the provided check.py to verify if your solution is correct. You will be tested on other positions as well.\n"], "completed": true, "concurrent_cells_at_end": 4, "concurrent_cells_at_start": 4, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "embedded_version": "2.0.50", "ended_et": "2026-11-12T17:56:11.739806-05:00", "ended_on_rejection": false, "endpoint_location": "global", "endpoint_location_mixed": false, "env_cause": null, "env_failure": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "failure_subclass": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "final_workspace_bytes": 244408, "final_workspace_skip_reason": null, "final_workspace_status": "saved", "final_workspace_tar": "/h2/drift-5140-1103/opus/5140/transcripts/with/opencode_regex-chess_claude-opus-5-5_trial4.workspace.tar.gz", "final_workspace_tar_bytes": 23371, "final_workspace_tar_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "free_disk_gb": 37.46, "fresh_subagents": 0, "functional_pass": null, "gate_cell": false, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170344 (/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "<HOST>", "image_digest": null, "image_scan_copies": [], "installed_anthropic": "2.0.50", "instance_id": "8187537343833955709", "instruction_app_rewrite": true, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "load_proof": "pass", "load_proof_basis": "user_agent", "load_proof_reason": "User-Agent 2.0.50", "loaded_anthropic": "2.0.50", "lock_wait_s": 0.0, "lockfile": "bun.lock", "lockfile_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "machine": "<HOST>", "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_match_reason": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "network_mode": "local", "off_protocol": false, "opencode_cache": "/h1/opencode-src", "output_tail": " rook or king moves, or a rook is captured\n- promotions, including promoting by capturing a rook\n\n**Speed:** each position takes about 0.5 seconds, almost all of it Python compiling the 2,000-odd regexes.\n\n**Known gap:** a checkmate or stalemate position (no legal moves) can't pass the checker. Splitting any string on newlines always gives at least one item, so the result can never be an empty list. The checker never tests these positions in the Opera Game.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. **Set-up:** the position is rewritten into a fixed-width form, with empty squares spelled out as dots, the castling rights as four fixed slots, and the en-passant square as two characters. That puts every square at a known offset in the string.\n2. **Generating moves:** each possible from/to square pair for each piece gets one regex. If the pattern matches (right piece, target not a white piece, path clear), it adds a new line holding the resulting position. Double pawn pushes set the en-passant square, and pawns reaching the last rank become queens. There are separate rules for en passant and for castling, which needs the right still held and the squares between empty.\n3. **Removing illegal moves:** one regex per square deletes any line where the white king on that square is attacked by a knight, pawn, king or sliding piece with a clear path. For castling, the squares the king starts on and passes over are marked so the same check also rejects castling out of or through check.\n4. **Castling rights:** a right is kept only if the king and that rook are still on their starting squares, which matches how python-chess reports them.\n5. **Output:** runs of dots go back to digits, \" b\" is added, and the castling and en-passant fields are tidied. The en-passant square is shown after every double push. The checker accepts that even when python-chess shows \"-\".\n\nI also left two helper scripts in the folder: `gen.py` rebuilds `re.json`, and `test.py` runs the random-game comparison against python-chess.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "pin_source": "override", "pin_source_class": "override", "probe_method": "embedded", "protocol_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "provider_loaded_mismatch": null, "provider_loaded_source": "embedded", "provider_loaded_version": "2.0.50", "provider_pin_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "provider_trace": "off", "provider_version_proven": true, "provider_version_source": "embedded", "provider_versions": {"@ai-sdk/anthropic": "2.0.50"}, "proxy_cost_usd": 1.6451842, "proxy_observed": [{"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null